{"id": "2d5b14a8-067a-4218-b6d6-7b9a0b1d962c", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T13:19:25.712669", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "8955bd20-8593-485a-b73b-bed364c9f234", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-d4c7219d-1627-4f8c-98b9-f91187a73484", "tool_call": {"id": "call-d4c7219d-1627-4f8c-98b9-f91187a73484", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose plan for PPO vs Q-Learning in SMAX\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"## 1. Workspace inspection — what is present and any constraints\\n\\nObserved:\\n- `/workspace` contains only `task.json` (question + design-only directive). No source code, no cloned repositories, no datasets, no readmes.\\n- `/home/actor` is empty. No JAX/JaxMARL/SMAX installed (`pip3 show jax jaxmarl` returns \\\"not found\\\").\\n- Network is **disabled**, so I cannot clone JaxMARL or fetch any docs/papers. PyPI/git commands are unavailable for this brief.\\n- Python 3.12.3 available; `git`, `wget`, `curl` are present but unusable for fetching.\\n- Environment spec: 24 CPU cores visible, GPU disabled, \\\"bubblewrap\\\" sandbox.\\n\\nConstraints this implies for the design:\\n- The design cannot assume I will read released JaxMARL hyperparameters, SMAX reward constants, or published score tables inline; it must treat those as **citation-required inputs the implementer retrieves**.\\n- No \\\"I ran it\\\" evidence is possible — all numbers in the final design document must be placeholders / illustrative.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Proposed high-level experimental approach\\n\\n### 2.1 Candidate SMAX maps / scenarios\\nPick three that span the difficulty / heterogeneity axis and are in JaxMARL's headline set:\\n- **3m** — homogeneous, symmetric, small (baseline / lower-difficulty).\\n- **3s_vs_5z** — heterogeneous unit types *and* asymmetric team sizes (test of credit assignment / sample efficiency).\\n- **5m_vs_6m** — asymmetric sizes, often harder convergence (tests off-policy advantage).\\n\\n(Add **2s_vs_1sc** as an optional fourth \\\"super-hard\\\" map if the budget allows; otherwise drop.)\\n\\n### 2.2 Algorithms under comparison\\n- **PPO branch (JaxMARL)**: use **MAPPO** as the primary PPO reference, because it is the strongest PPO in JaxMARL and the one reported in the JaxMARL paper. Run **IPPO** as a PPO ablation to clarify how much centralized critic is worth.\\n- **Q-Learning branch**: use **QMIX** as the primary Q-Learning reference. **VDN** and **IQL** run as Q-Learning-family ablations to attribute gains to credit assignment (mixing net) vs. off-policy per se.\\n\\n### 2.3 Shared vs. differing components\\n- **Shared**: JaxMARL's SMAX environment wrappers (e.g., `SMAXLogWrapper`), obs/action spaces, episode length, reward function (JaxMARL's default mixed sparse+shaped reward — to be confirmed against the JaxMARL repo at execution time), evaluation protocol, MLP body architecture (2-layer 64-unit ReLU), GRU encoder either **disabled in both** for the headline comparison (cleaner) or **enabled in both** (recurrent ablation), total environment step budget (e.g., 2×10⁶ steps per (algorithm, map, seed)).\\n- **Differing**: optimizer (Adam with algorithm-specific lr/clip), rollout-vs-replay data pipeline, target-network update schedule (Q-Learning only), central value head vs. mixing network — these are intrinsic to the algorithms and not \\\"balanced.\\\"\\n\\n### 2.4 Training-time and normalized-score measurement\\n\\n**Training time** — report **both**:\\n- *Wall-clock seconds to first reach a threshold normalized score* (e.g., 0.8 of expert); computed on a single fixed machine and a single fixed JAX backend (GPU if present, CPU otherwise — declared up front).\\n- *Environment steps to the same threshold* (hardware-portable secondary metric).\\n- Also report mean per-step wall-clock (µs / env step) and total wall-clock to budget cap.\\n\\n**Normalized score**:\\n- Per-episode shaped return from the configured reward.\\n- Define `normalized_score(τ) = (score(τ) − score_random) / (score_expert − score_random)` per (map). `score_random` from a no-op / uniform-random policy run on the same wrapper, same number of episodes (e.g., 32). `score_expert` either (a) the published JaxMARl-paper best score for that map, or (b) the best score observed across our own runs on the same hardware; the choice must be declared and **consistent across both algorithms** (head-to-head fairness).\\n- Aggregate: AUC of the learning curve (env-step-normalized), final-eval score (mean over last 100 eval episodes), and threshold-hit time.\\n\\n### 2.5 Controls\\n- **Seeds**: ≥ 5 independent seeds per (algorithm, map); 3 is the absolute floor.\\n- **Hardware normalization**: lock everything to one machine, one JAX backend, one process layout; record JAX backend string and device count in every run's metadata.\\n- **Environment wrappers**: identical across algorithms; identical eval episodes per checkpoint.\\n- **Network capacity**: identical MLP body in actors/critics/mixer-encoder; embed dimension constant.\\n- **Episode budgets**: identical total env steps; identical eval frequency; identical checkpoint cadence.\\n- **Hyperparameters**: start from JaxMARL defaults; deviations logged in a per-run override table.\\n- **Evaluation protocol**: deterministic policies (argmax for Q-Learning, mean for PPO) over a fixed set of eval seeds independent from training seeds.\\n\\n### 2.6 Analysis / comparison plan\\n- **Per-run outputs**: per-seed CSV of (env_step, wallclock, eval_return, normalized_score). Learning-curve plot with shaded 95% CI across seeds.\\n- **Aggregate tables**: per (algorithm × map) — mean ± 95% CI of (a) AUC normalized score, (b) wall-clock-to-threshold, (c) env-steps-to-threshold, (d) final normalized score.\\n- **Statistical tests**: Wilcoxon signed-rank test across the per-seed deltas (PPO − QMIX) on each metric, pooled per-map and per-metric; complement with bootstrap CIs. Holm-Bonferroni correction across the family of metrics.\\n- **Reporting format**: one results table per metric, one line plot per map, one summary paragraph.\\n- **Ablations**: (i) IPPO vs MAPPO (centralized-critic effect), (ii) IQL vs VDN vs QMIX (mixing-net effect), (iii) GRU on/off (recurrence effect), (iv) shared vs separate body encoder between actor and value/critic head.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\\n\\n### Assumptions (would lock if approved)\\n- A1. Compute budget sufficient for 5 seeds × 3 maps × {IPPO, MAPPO, IQL, VDN, QMIX} — that's 75 runs at 2×10⁶ steps each; will likely require a GPU and multi-day runtime.\\n- A2. Q-Learning primary = **QMIX**; PPO primary = **MAPPO**.\\n- A3. SMAX maps = **3m, 3s_vs_5z, 5m_vs_6m** (3 maps, fixed).\\n- A4. Identical MLP body (2×64, ReLU); **no GRU** in the headline comparison; GRU as a separate ablation.\\n- A5. Identical total env-step budget per (run) and identical eval/ckpt cadence.\\n- A6. Training time measured as wall-clock on a fixed single-machine JAX backend (GPU if present), AND simultaneously as env-steps-to-threshold for portability.\\n- A7. Reward function = JaxMARl SMAX defaults (sparse + shaped, **to verify** against the repo at execution).\\n- A8. \\\"Normalized score\\\" uses a self-measured random baseline; \\\"expert\\\" baseline is either JaxMARL-paper published numbers OR the best observed across our own runs, whichever is more defensible for fairness at design time — the choice must be the same for both algorithms.\\n- A9. Deterministic eval using argmax (Q-Learning) / mean (PPO) over fixed eval seeds.\\n- A10. No shared-encoder trick in headline runs; flagged as a separate ablation.\\n\\n### Uncertainties / decisions the researcher should make\\n- U1. Is MAPPO acceptable as the \\\"PPO\\\" arm, or must the comparison be IPPO-only (which is weaker and arguably unfair to PPO on cooperative tasks)?\\n- U2. Is QMIX acceptable as \\\"Q-Learning,\\\" or should the comparison extend to C/WQMIX or SHAQ-equivalents that also leverage the centralized critic (a more even match to MAPPO)?\\n- U3. How many seeds: 3 vs 5 vs 10 (3 is underpowered, 10 may bust the compute budget)?\\n- U4. Hardware and compute budget to declare up front so the design document can state runtime expectations precisely.\\n- U5. Exact env-step budget per run (2e6 vs 5e6 vs until plateau) — drives runtime directly.\\n- U6. Threshold for \\\"time-to-score\\\" (e.g., 0.6, 0.7, 0.8 of expert?) — sensitivity to this choice should be reported.\\n- U7. Whether to declare which fields of the global state the QMIX mixer hypernet sees (SMAX exposes it; this is a known advantage that biases the comparison in Q-Learning's favor and should be acknowledged, not removed).\\n- U8. Whether the implementer should pin specific JaxMARL config files (algorithms/smax/{ipo,mappo,qmix,...}/...) verbatim or re-tune; my recommendation is pin-and-report unless a brief smoke test shows defaults are broken.\\n- U9. Whether to include a per-map learning-curve figure and a per-map CI table, or a single aggregate-with-metric figure — affects how progress is communicated.\\n\\nI will wait for explicit approval (and answers/decisions on at least U1–U6) before producing the full stage=result design document.\",\"evidence\":\"Findings under evidence constraints: (i) Workspace inspection via `inspect_repository` and `execute_check` shows `/workspace` contains only `task.json`; `/home/actor` and `/tmp` are empty; `pip3 show jax jaxmarl` ⇒ \\\"Package(s) not found\\\"; `task.json` declares repositories/compute out of scope and `runtime=disabled-network`. (ii) Algorithm and SMAX-map choices are based on prior knowledge of the JaxMARL paper (Rutherford et al. 2024), which reports MAPPO/QMIX/IPPO/IQL/VDN baselines on SMAX maps including 3m, 3s_vs_5z, 5m_vs_6m; QMIX is the literature-standard strongest credit-assigning off-policy baseline for cooperative MARL (Rashid et al. 2018/2020); MAPPO is the strongest PPO baseline for cooperative MARL (Yu et al. 2022). (iii) Because the design-only directive forbids claiming a run, no numbers from a real experiment are cited.\",\"assumptions\":\"See section 3 of the plan (A1–A10): 5 seeds × 3 maps × 5 algorithms; QMIX as primary Q-Learning; MAPPO as primary PPO; identical MLP body, no GRU in headline; fixed JAX backend; wall-clock + env-step dual reporting; JaxMARL-default reward; self-measured random + JaxMARL-paper-or-our-best expert normalization.\",\"uncertainties\":\"See section 3 U1–U9: MAPPO vs IPPO allowance, QMIX vs SHAQ/CWQMIX allowance, seed count, hardware/budget, env-step budget, threshold for time-to-score, treatment of state-conditioned mixer as a bias, whether to pin JaxMARL defaults verbatim or re-tune, reporting granularity. Awaiting researcher direction on at least U1–U6 before producing stage=result.\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-bc87d980-0b35-436a-a0ec-8264a0528f12", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 18}
