: Wilcoxon signed-rank across per-seed deltas (PPO \\u2212 QMIX) on each metric, per map; complement with bootstrap CIs. Holm-Bonferroni correction across the family of metrics.\\n- **Reporting format**: one results table per metric, one line plot per map, one summary paragraph.\\n- **Ablations**: (i) IPPO vs MAPPO (centralized-critic effect), (ii) IQL vs VDN vs QMIX (mixing-net effect), (iii) GRU on/off (recurrence effect), (iv) shared vs separate body encoder between actor and value/critic head.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\\n\\n### Assumptions (would lock if approved)\\n- A1. Compute budget sufficient for 5 seeds \\u00d7 3 maps \\u00d7 {IPPO, MAPPO, IQL, VDN, QMIX} \\u2014 that's 75 runs at 2\\u00d710\\u2076 steps each; will likely require a GPU and multi-day runtime.\\n- A2. Q-Learning primary = **QMIX**; PPO primary = **MAPPO**.\\n- A3. SMAX maps = **3m, 3s_vs_5z, 5m_vs_6m** (3 maps, fixed).\\n- A4. Identical MLP body (2\\u00d764, ReLU); **no GRU** in the headline comparison; GRU as a separate ablation.\\n- A5. Identical total env-step budget per (run) and identical eval/ckpt cadence.\\n- A6. Training time measured as wall-clock on a fixed single-machine JAX backend (GPU if present) **and** as env-steps-to-threshold for portability.\\n- A7. Reward function = JaxMARL SMAX defaults (sparse + shaped, **to verify** against the repo at execution).\\n- A8. \\\"Normalized score\\\" uses a self-measured random baseline; \\\"expert\\\" baseline is either JaxMARL-paper published numbers OR the best across our own runs \\u2014 whichever is chosen, it is the same for both algorithms.\\n- A9. Deterministic eval using argmax (Q-Learning) / mean (PPO) over fixed eval seeds.\\n- A10. No shared-encoder trick in headline runs; flagged as a separate ablation.\\n\\n### Uncertainties / decisions the researcher should make\\n- U1. Is MAPPO acceptable as the \\\"PPO\\\" arm, or must the comparison be IPPO-only (IPPO is weaker and arguably unfair to PPO on cooperative tasks)?\\n- U2. Is QMIX acceptable as \\\"Q-Learning,\\\" or should the comparison extend to C/WQMIX or SHAQ-equivalents that also leverage a centralized critic (a more even match to MAPPO)?\\n- U3. How many seeds: 3 vs 5 vs 10 (3 is underpowered, 10 may bust the compute budget)?\\n- U4. Hardware and compute budget to declare up front so the design document can state runtime expectations precisely.\\n- U5. Exact env-step budget per run (2e6 vs 5e6 vs until plateau) \\u2014 drives runtime directly.\\n- U6. Threshold for \\\"time-to-score\\\" (e.g., 0.6, 0.7, 0.8 of expert?) \\u2014 sensitivity to this choice should be reported.\\n- U7. Whether to declare which fields of the global state the QMIX mixer hypernet sees (SMAX exposes it; this biases the comparison in Q-Learning's favor and should be acknowledged, not removed).\\n- U8. Whether to pin specific JaxMARL config files (algorithms/smax/{ippo,m apppo,qmix,...}) verbatim or re-tune; my recommendation is pin-and-report unless a brief smoke test shows defaults are broken.\\n- U9. Reporting granularity: one figure per map or one aggregate-with-metric figure \\u2014 affects how progress is communicated.\\n\\nI will wait for explicit approval (and decisions on at least U1\\u2013U6) before producing the full stage=result design document.\", \"evidence\": \"Findings under evidence constraints: (i) Workspace inspection via `inspect_repository` and `execute_check` shows `/workspace` contains only `task.json`; `/home/actor` and `/tmp` are empty; `pip3 show jax jaxmarl` returns \\\"Package(s) not found\\\"; `task.json` declares repositories/compute out of scope and `runtime=disabled-network`. (ii) Algorithm and SMAX-map choices are based on prior knowledge of the JaxMARL paper (Rutherford et al. 2024), which reports MAPPO/QMIX/IPPO/IQL/VDN baselines on SMAX maps including 3m, 3s_vs_5z, 5m_vs_6m; QMIX is the literature-standard strongest credit-assigning off-policy baseline for cooperative MARL (Rashid et al. 2018/2020); MAPPO is the strongest PPO baseline for cooperative MARL (Yu et al. 2022). (iii) Because the design-only directive forbids claiming a run, no numbers from a real experiment are cited.\", \"assumptions\": [\"A1. 5 seeds \\u00d7 3 maps \\u00d7 5 algorithms (IPPO, MAPPO, IQL, VDN, QMIX) = 75 runs; GPU + multi-day runtime expected.\", \"A2. Q-Learning primary = QMIX; PPO primary = MAPPO.\", \"A3. SMAX maps = 3m, 3s_vs_5z, 5m_vs_6m.\", \"A4. Identical MLP body (2\\u00d764, ReLU); no GRU in headline; GRU as ablation.\", \"A5. Identical env-step budget, eval/ckpt cadence.\", \"A6. Wall-clock on fixed JAX backend + env-steps-to-threshold both reported.\", \"A7. JaxMARL-default SMAX reward (verify at execution).\", \"A8. Random baseline self-measured; expert baseline = JaxMARL-paper OR our-best, applied identically to both algorithms.\", \"A9. Deterministic eval: argmax for Q-Learning, mean for PPO, fixed eval seeds.\", \"A10. No shared-encoder trick in headline runs (only as ablation).\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-767bc6a1-d2dc-481b-8486-7c682f6101ef", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 20}
